---
import Footer from "@/components/layout/Footer.astro";
import PageLayout from "@/components/layout/PageLayout.astro";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
	title="Contact Railly Hugo | railly.dev"
	description="Official contact information for Railly Hugo, software engineer, open-source maintainer, speaker, and founder of Crafter Station."
>
	<PageLayout class="flex flex-col gap-10">
		<header class="space-y-4">
			<h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Contact Railly Hugo</h1>
			<p class="max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-foreground-2">
				The canonical contact address for Railly Hugo and railly.dev is
				<a href="mailto:hi@railly.dev" class="ml-1 underline decoration-ui underline-offset-4">hi@railly.dev</a>.
				Use it for collaboration, speaking, open-source work, developer tools,
				AI research, mentoring, press, or corrections to this website. Include a
				clear subject, the relevant project or page, and the action you are requesting.
			</p>
		</header>
		<section class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-foreground-2">
			<h2 class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wider">Where to write</h2>
			<p class="max-w-2xl">
				For public technical work, prefer the matching GitHub repository so the
				discussion remains searchable and useful to contributors. For security reports,
				follow <a href="/.well-known/security.txt" class="underline">security.txt</a>
				and avoid publishing exploit details before remediation. This personal site
				does not provide emergency support, a public phone number, or guaranteed response times.
			</p>
			<ul class="space-y-2">
				<li><a class="underline" href="https://github.com/Railly">GitHub: @Railly</a></li>
				<li><a class="underline" href="https://linkedin.com/in/railly-hugo">LinkedIn: Railly Hugo</a></li>
				<li><a class="underline" href="https://x.com/raillyhugo">X: @raillyhugo</a></li>
			</ul>
		</section>
		<Footer />
	</PageLayout>
</Layout>
